Subject: [PATCH 09/11] fix(#94): FileIdentity and RevisionId, landed by
 TEST_BASIS B1 and never instantiated, are retired

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "a computed field no reader reads is invisible". `regime.FileIdentity`
(dev, ino) and `regime.RevisionId` (content and context digest) were landed ahead of their consumers
("Land the identity types ... No deletions") and no code ever built one.

Why the obvious fix is wrong: wiring them where B1 points would add a second spelling of questions that
are already answered. The live-session question ("is this the same open file") is asked in
`engine._same_file` / `_import_identity`, which use `os.path.samefile` and cannot import `regime` (regime
imports engine; a cycle). The across-run question has no consumer: the verdict cache keys on the content
digests it already carries. So both are deleted; `TestId` and `ModuleId` stay. The comment in regime.py and
the B1 row of docs/TEST_BASIS.md say so, since both described them as landed.

Not closed: the other 6 OPEN fields.

OPEN 10 -> 6. Disarmed (types restored), the new intent test fails (1 of 1). Guards and regime tests pass
under 3.14 and 3.12 apart from the unrelated `bound` entry; ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
